---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TravelCTA from "../components/TravelCTA.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Hair Transplant in India | CareBridge Health"
  description="Affordable, high-quality hair transplant surgery in India with CareBridge Health. FUE / DHI, natural hairline design, transparent costs and full travel coordination for international patients."
>
  <main class="container mx-auto px-5 py-12 max-w-5xl">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700 mb-2">
        Hair Transplant · International Patients
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        Hair Transplant in India with clear planning and support
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 max-w-3xl">
        We help patients from the Middle East, Europe and Asia get safe, 
        well-planned hair transplant surgery in India. You get guidance before 
        you fly, coordination during your stay, and follow-up after you return home.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          href="https://wa.me/919080553616?text=Hi%2C%20I%20want%20to%20know%20if%20I%20am%20a%20good%20candidate%20for%20hair%20transplant."
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition"
        >
          Send photos on WhatsApp
        </a>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
          Free initial opinion · No obligation to book
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- QUICK HIGHLIGHTS -->
    <section class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3 mb-14 text-sm">
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">FUE / DHI techniques</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">
          Modern extraction methods with focus on natural hairline, density and
          donor area protection.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">Transparent planning</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">
          Approximate graft range, sessions required and stay length shared before you commit.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-900 mb-1">End-to-end coordination</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-600">
          Help with dates, airport pick-up, language support and basic after-care instructions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CANDIDATE CHECK -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">
        Are you a good candidate for hair transplant?
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        Not everyone with hair loss should immediately do a transplant. 
        First we look at your current pattern, age, family history and donor area.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2">Usually good candidates</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Men with stable pattern (Norwood 3–5) and strong donor density</li>
            <li>Previous transplant needing density or hairline correction</li>
            <li>Eyebrow / beard restoration with realistic expectations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-rose-100 bg-rose-50/60 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-2 text-rose-800">We may advise “not yet” or “no” if</h3>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Hair loss is very early and still rapidly progressing</li>
            <li>Donor area is weak or over-harvested from past surgery</li>
            <li>You expect “full teenage density” from one session</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-rose-900/80">
            Saying “no” is part of our job. Long-term result is more important than selling a package.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TECHNIQUES -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">
        Techniques and planning approach
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        The exact method is decided by the surgeon after examining you in 
        person, but we usually talk about these options during the online assessment:
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">FUE (Follicular Unit Extraction)</h3>
          <p>
            Individual grafts are taken from the donor area with tiny punches. 
            Good for most male-pattern hair loss cases with sufficient donor.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">DHI / Implanter-based placement</h3>
          <p>
            Variation of FUE where grafts are placed using implanter pens. 
            Helps with dense packing in selected areas when done correctly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Medical therapy + transplant combo</h3>
          <p>
            In many patients we combine transplant with medical treatment 
            (where safe) to protect existing hair and slow future loss.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- COST & STAY -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">
        Cost &amp; typical stay in India
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        Exact cost depends on grafts, technique, city and clinic, but these 
        ranges help you decide if travelling makes sense.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Grafts</h3>
          <p class="mb-1">Most cases: <span class="font-medium">2,000–4,000 grafts</span></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
            Higher counts may need two days or staged sessions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Stay length</h3>
          <p>Typical visit: <span class="font-medium">5–7 days</span></p>
          <ul class="mt-1 list-disc list-inside text-xs space-y-1">
            <li>Day 1: consult + tests</li>
            <li>Day 2: surgery</li>
            <li>Day 3–5: wash &amp; checks</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-100 p-4">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Cost advantage</h3>
          <p>
            Many international patients save around 
            <span class="font-medium">50–70% vs. their home country</span>, 
            even after flights and hotel, while using accredited hospitals.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-slate-500">
        We’ll give you a personalised range after seeing your photos and medical history. 
        Final quote always comes from the treating clinic, not from CareBridge alone.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- VIDEO SECTION -->
    <section class="mb-14">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">
        Watch: How the CareBridge hair transplant journey works
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">
        This short video explains the full process – from first WhatsApp message 
        to flying back home after surgery.
      </p>

      <div class="relative w-full pt-[56.25%] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden bg-black/80">
        <iframe
          class="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full"
          src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/RUMWGaiIBXI"
          title="Hair transplant journey explainer"
          frameborder="0"
          allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
          allowfullscreen
        ></iframe>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        Hair transplant FAQs
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
        <details class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">
            When will I see full results?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Most patients see shedding in the first month, visible growth from 
            month 3–4, and the main result around month 9–12. Final refinement 
            can continue up to 18 months.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">
            Will people notice I had a transplant?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2">
            In the first 10–14 days, yes – there will be redness and scabs. 
            After that it looks like a short buzz-cut. Once the hair grows, 
            a properly designed hairline should look natural in normal social distance.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">
            Can you guarantee a specific number of grafts or density?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2">
            No one can honestly guarantee exact graft numbers or final density 
            before seeing you in person. We share a realistic range and ask the 
            clinic to confirm after physical examination.
          </p>
        </details>

        <details class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-4">
          <summary class="font-semibold cursor-pointer">
            What happens if I change my mind after the online assessment?
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Nothing. The initial WhatsApp discussion and case review are free. 
            You should only travel if you genuinely feel comfortable with the plan.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Travel CTA from shared component -->
    <TravelCTA />
  </main>
</Layout>
